{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"07612fcb3ba1cb5c557323c593e76e557769ce6c190a4a18245f4ba29326df9c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_75da86e635800f603fa3a8a1b5e7379cd1e08ac514eaf6146b7e7d27cc451c9f","overall_assessment":"The paper is technically sound but fails to adhere to double-blind review policies by including author names and affiliations. Data usage is compliant with standard research practices, and there are no signs of plagiarism. The absence of ethical and broader impact discussions is noted but is consistent with the 2017 venue requirements.","paper_id":"BJAA4wKxg","paper_identity_sha256":"98b9b4176df4f72beb21d3969ba8447c971f22081a8c01be2d130e86e6c2da37","prompt_identity_sha256":"31a4c479b19d8e1f4e3ac786bae4f19e41deb39442e4bcf08b862e92da02f740","raw_response_sha256":"bccd119b6174e1bd88ebc7997ad235facee06cd911621b3d817e3eac0c4f9c22","request_identity_sha256":"8c73c3fa6f3d5979ffab440be0b6089630a8d7c1babaf0539f89656ae93ada3b","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential societal harms. While the work focuses on a technical architectural improvement for machine translation, there is no discussion regarding bias in the translation models, potential misuse, or the impact on marginalized language communities. Given the 2017 context, a broader impact statement was not yet a standard requirement for ICLR, but the absence of any ethical consideration is noted.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes standard public benchmarks (IWSLT'14, WMT'14, WMT'15, WMT'16) and explicitly cites the sources for the data (e.g., Cettolo et al., 2014; Schwenk, 2014; Sennrich et al., 2016b). The datasets mentioned (Europarl, Common Crawl, News Commentary) are widely used in the NLP community and are generally available under licenses that permit research use. The paper does not report any privacy violations or use of non-public, sensitive personal data. The data usage appears compliant with standard research practices of the time.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors (Jonas Gehring, Michael Auli, David Grangier, Yann N. Dauphin) and their affiliation (Facebook AI Research) on the title page. This is a clear violation of double-blind review policies, which require the removal of author names and affiliations to prevent bias during the review process. The presence of this information compromises the anonymity of the submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-012"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work extensively, including concurrent work by Kalchbrenner et al. (2016) and Lamb & Xie (2016). There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the visible text. The content appears to be original, with proper attribution to foundational works in neural machine translation and convolutional networks.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-032","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which were not mandatory for ICLR 2017 submissions. However, the work has clear positive implications for the efficiency and accessibility of machine translation technology. The lack of explicit discussion on the broader societal impact is a limitation, though consistent with the norms of the venue and year. No software or data licenses are explicitly stated beyond the citation of the datasets and the use of the Torch framework.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"3a80bf2397d83da8fa3104fb4095bfd59ef934d8f658c85f283aed5f55c57ba3","paper_id":"BJAA4wKxg","paper_ordinal":24,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"bccd119b6174e1bd88ebc7997ad235facee06cd911621b3d817e3eac0c4f9c22","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJAA4wKxg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"f3c2e7902aac7060c471b26c1ceba65687e3f4c7bbad69f3547c6d27fee4fb46","request_identity_sha256":"8c73c3fa6f3d5979ffab440be0b6089630a8d7c1babaf0539f89656ae93ada3b","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":828,"prompt_tokens":18158,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18986},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"8c73c3fa6f3d5979ffab440be0b6089630a8d7c1babaf0539f89656ae93ada3b","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}